sequenceDiagram
    %% Multi-cluster GitOps reconciliation — the ApplicationSet matrix pattern in motion.

    actor Dev as Platform Engineer
    participant Git as GitHub<br/>(source of truth)
    participant AS as ApplicationSet<br/>bls-workloads<br/>(matrix generator)
    participant ArgoCD as ArgoCD controller<br/>(in-cluster on k3s)
    participant K3s as k3s cluster<br/>(homelab)
    participant AKS as AKS cluster<br/>(bls-aks-demo)

    Dev->>Git: git push to main<br/>(values.yaml change)
    Git-->>AS: webhook OR ArgoCD polls<br/>(3-min reconcile interval)
    Note over AS: Matrix generator:<br/>[clusters] × [workloads]<br/>= N Applications

    AS->>ArgoCD: generates Applications<br/>llm-gateway-in-cluster<br/>llm-gateway-bls-aks-demo<br/>(+ other workloads)

    par Reconcile to k3s
        ArgoCD->>K3s: helm template + kubectl apply
        K3s-->>ArgoCD: resource status<br/>(Synced / Healthy)
    and Reconcile to AKS
        ArgoCD->>AKS: helm template + kubectl apply
        AKS-->>ArgoCD: resource status<br/>(Synced / Healthy)
    end

    ArgoCD-->>Dev: UI shows<br/>both child apps Synced/Healthy

    Note over ArgoCD,AKS: selfHeal=true: any manual drift<br/>in either cluster is reverted<br/>within minutes.

%% Caption — supports BLS-PLATFORM-ENGINEERING-GUIDE.md §4 (P3 multi-cluster
%% GitOps) and ADR-005 (ApplicationSet matrix pattern). The diagram shows the
%% full reconciliation cycle for a single git push: ApplicationSet expands the
%% matrix into one Application per (cluster × workload) pair, ArgoCD reconciles
%% each Application to its target cluster in parallel, and health rolls back up.
%% The closing note captures why selfHeal=true is load-bearing — drift in
%% either cluster is a bug, and ArgoCD is the mechanism that treats it as one.
